### Smart Expense Tracker API — Sample Requests

@baseUrl = http://127.0.0.1:8000
@token = PASTE_YOUR_ACCESS_TOKEN_HERE

### 1. API health check
GET {{baseUrl}}/

### 2. Register a new user
POST {{baseUrl}}/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "demo@example.com",
  "password": "DemoPass123!"
}

### 3. Login
POST {{baseUrl}}/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "demo@example.com",
  "password": "DemoPass123!"
}

### 4. Get authenticated user
GET {{baseUrl}}/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 5. List categories
GET {{baseUrl}}/categories
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 6. Create an expense transaction
POST {{baseUrl}}/transactions
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "amount_paise": 20000,
  "type": "expense",
  "date": "2026-10-20",
  "note": "Lunch",
  "payment_method": "cash",
  "category_id": 1
}

### 7. List transactions
GET {{baseUrl}}/transactions
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 8. Filter transactions by date range
GET {{baseUrl}}/transactions?start_date=2026-10-01&end_date=2026-10-20
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 9. Get custom-range report
GET {{baseUrl}}/reports/summary?start_date=2026-10-01&end_date=2026-10-20
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 10. Get monthly report
GET {{baseUrl}}/reports/monthly
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 11. AI transaction categorization
POST {{baseUrl}}/ai/categorize
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "description": "Paid 200 rupees for lunch"
}

### 12. Validation test — zero amount should be rejected
POST {{baseUrl}}/transactions
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "amount_paise": 0,
  "type": "expense",
  "date": "2026-10-20",
  "note": "Invalid amount test",
  "payment_method": "cash",
  "category_id": 1
}
